# LF in the working directory and in history, on every platform, whatever the
# local `core.autocrlf` says.
#
# This is not cosmetic here. The files under `templates/` are read as text and
# their bytes are what a scaffolded project receives, so a CRLF checkout would
# change what this plugin hands another project — and the map reader measures
# sections in bytes, so a checkout could move a section across the size limit.
* text=auto eol=lf
